  "notes": [
    "Rows reuse exact matching sample UUIDs and the repository TranscriptScorer; existing passing baseline inference was not repeated.",
    "Raw CER includes punctuation, capitalization, and written-number formatting. Supplementary content-character counts use NFC, lowercase, and alphanumeric-only text identically for every backend; no raw metric or gate was replaced.",
    "The public-human profiles contain 24 samples per language. The mixed-language subset contains only two synthetic samples and is not a release holdout.",
    "The original 64-sample Whisper run produced four empty prompted speech results, 17 dangerous-token errors, and hallucinations on both non-speech samples; its P95 was 1850.386333 ms and RTF 0.11812943645357413.",
    "Removing prompts for the four empty cases restored nonempty speech but still left three dangerous-token gate errors. Disabling only the first-token log-probability early-exit heuristic on all five prompted cases did not repair the empty results; that unsuccessful configuration change was removed.",
    "No claim is made that this tests every Whisper model or configuration. The SDK's separate auto-download tokenizer fallback remains blocked by the parent sandbox. No user recording, transcript, dictionary, or identity was sent to a network service."
